From f81b82a22ec9100d4ed3f20f1f7139921d077e29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?A=CC=82nderson=20Q?= <anquadros@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 12:27:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] theme: Move per-window theme swap out of gpui core

Address review feedback on the per-window theme override design: instead of
threading a draw observer and a global-mutation-without-notify escape hatch
through gpui, the active theme now lives in GlobalTheme behind a RefCell and
is set once per frame from Workspace::render, before anything reads
cx.theme(). gpui itself is untouched.

ActiveTheme::theme() now returns an owned Arc<Theme> instead of a borrowed
reference, which is why this diff is larger than the theme crate alone: every
call site chaining a method off the old reference needed a let binding, and a
few passed cx.theme() directly where a &Theme was expected.
